<task id="112" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>ISS-022 (#1001) — a stale snapshot of the grant rows must not let the duplicate collapse SHORTEN access</title>
    <phase>Register-driven (queued 2026-09-18 by owner directive)</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Grant write path (.cs, Api/ExternalAccess); tags bff-api/auth; modifies tests; the primary fix reaches into the shared Dataverse client.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>RE-TIERED from `sonnet` on verification. The stub's reason — "a localized concurrency fix on one endpoint" — is FALSE: the register's own suggested fix (`If-Match`) is not implementable without adding precondition support to `DataverseWebApiClient` (`:204-214` has no header hook) and an etag field to `ExternalGrantRow` (`:78-120` has none), i.e. a change to a SHARED library whose `DeactivateAsync` is also called by the revoke path (`RevokeExternalAccessEndpoint.cs:152`). Cross-request concurrency with correctness consequences on two write paths — the same profile as task 103, which was opus.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Api/ExternalAccess/** is parallel-unsafe in this project; this also touches src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse, which every BFF write path uses.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>106</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>5–7 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Register ISS-022 / GitHub #1001. Filed by task 106 Step 9.5 code-review finding F5. Queued by the owner's 2026-09-18 directive. Authored 2026-09-19 with premises re-verified against HEAD — the defect is real; the suggested FIX was under-scoped, see `&lt;notes&gt;`.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>`GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.CreateGrantAsync` reads the key's active rows (`:204`), elects a survivor (`:215`), writes it (`:260`), then deactivates the rest (`:321` → `:478` → `ExternalGrantLifecycle.DeactivateAsync` `:416`) — with NO ETag and no conditional update anywhere between the read and the writes. Task 106 moved the election key from the IMMUTABLE `sprk_externalrecordaccessid` to the MUTABLE `sprk_expiresdate`, read at T₀ (`ConferralRank`, `ExternalGrantLifecycle.cs:217-218`; ordered at `:252-255`), which makes one new outcome reachable.

Rows r₁ (expires today+10, lower id) and r₂ (today+200). A date-less grant reads both and elects r₂. Concurrently `POST …/set-record-share-expiry` moves r₂ to today+1 (it writes ONLY `sprk_expiresdate` — `SetRecordShareExpiryEndpoint.cs:213-216`). The grant then collapses onto r₂ — now the SHORTER row — and deactivates r₁. The union conferred access until +10 before the call and until +1 after. Pre-106 the same interleaving elected r₁ and kept +10.

⚠️ The two writers use DIFFERENT Dataverse clients: the collapse PATCHes through `DataverseWebApiClient`, the expiry setter goes through `IDataverseService.BulkUpdateAsync` (`DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:2327`). They share no transaction. A row-version precondition still DETECTS the other writer; nothing can make them coordinate, so do not try.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, C#/.NET, the external grant lifecycle.</role>
  <goal>A duplicate collapse cannot apply to a row whose state changed since the read, so a concurrent expiry change cannot shorten conferred access and a concurrent revoke cannot leave the key with zero active rows. Every outcome the endpoint cannot verify is reported as such rather than as success.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Task 106 fixed a false 409 by electing the row that confers access longest. That election is deliberately REQUEST-INDEPENDENT and structurally so: `ElectSurvivor(IReadOnlyList&lt;ExternalGrantRow&gt;, DateOnly)` (`ExternalGrantLifecycle.cs:245`) has no parameter through which a request value could be reintroduced, because a request-parameterised order let two racers elect different survivors and deactivate each other, leaving ZERO active rows (finding V1/F1; the reasoning is preserved at `:195-215` and `notes/task-106-regrant-expired-survivor.md:203`). This task must not undo that.

**What the suggested fix actually costs — verified, because the register makes it sound like one line.** "`If-Match` on the row's ETag" needs three pieces that do not exist:
  1. `ExternalGrantRow` (`ExternalGrantLifecycle.cs:78-120`) has no `@odata.etag` property, and `RowSelect` (`:261-264`) does not request one — the row version is never read today.
  2. `DataverseWebApiClient.UpdateAsync` (`:204-214`) is `(entitySetName, id, entity, ct)` and builds its own request via `CreateAuthenticatedRequestAsync` (`:161-167`), which sets only `Authorization`. There is no If-Match support anywhere in that client (the repo's other If-Match uses are Compose/Graph and Cosmos, not this client).
  3. Nothing handles a 412. `UpdateAsync` calls `EnsureSuccessStatusCode()`, so a precondition failure surfaces as a bare `HttpRequestException`.

Ripple: `DeactivateAsync` has a SECOND caller, `RevokeExternalAccessEndpoint.cs:152`. A required-precondition signature changes the revoke path too; an optional one does not. Decide deliberately.

Current error posture to preserve or change deliberately: `CollapseDuplicatesAsync` SWALLOWS failures (`:480-485`) because the caller's grant already succeeded, while `DeactivateAsync` PROPAGATES (`:403-404`) so a partial sweep surfaces. A 412 arriving in the swallowing branch would be silently discarded — which is precisely the shape this task exists to remove.</background>
