  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="register ISS-022">Scope: the diagnosis. Task 106's V1 fix does NOT address this. V1 removed request-DEPENDENCE from the ranking; this is about the ranked column being MUTABLE. Do not "fix" the election.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 106">Scope: the election. Do NOT reintroduce request-dependence. `ElectSurvivor` takes no request value so the property is structural, not checked; perturbation P5 pins it. A concurrency fix must not add a parameter through which a request value could re-enter.</constraint>
    <constraint source="register ISS-022">Scope: honest coverage. Only the SHORTENING shape is new. The revoke-race variant — a racer deactivates the elected row, then the collapse removes the others, leaving ZERO active rows — is PRE-EXISTING and symmetric (pre-106 it fired whenever the revoked row was the lowest id). Fix both, or state in the notes which is out of scope and why.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: fail direction. An outcome the endpoint cannot verify is never reported as success. A discarded 412 is exactly that — if the precondition path lands inside the currently-swallowing `CollapseDuplicatesAsync` catch (`:480-485`), the swallow must become deliberate and distinguishable, not inherited.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: the shared client. `src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse` is consumed by every BFF write path. Any precondition support must be ADDITIVE and default to today's behaviour, so no existing caller changes semantics by being recompiled. State the placement decision explicitly in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Scope: new surface. Extend the existing `UpdateAsync` with an optional precondition rather than adding a parallel client or a second write path. One way to PATCH a row, not two.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Scope: refusal shape. Any new client-visible refusal is ProblemDetails with a stable reason code and the trace id, matching the file's existing codes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="review-2026-08-24">Scope: verification. Perturbation is mandatory; pair positives with negatives.</constraint>
    <constraint source="risk-register (plan §7)">Scope: the instrument. A green single-request suite is NOT evidence here. Task 106 passed build, 51/51 tests and 4/4 perturbations over a real privilege-loss defect because every instrument was single-request and the defect lived BETWEEN two requests. The test for this must span two writers interleaved at the read/write boundary, or it does not test this at all.</constraint>
  </constraints>

